WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.300
Accessibility coordinator: Did the wiki make it into the accessibility audit?

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.800
IT director: Not yet. It is thousands of pages.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.800
Accessibility coordinator: What does a screen reader say on them?

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.400
IT director: “Graphic.” Look at this.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.300
A normal wiki page. Nothing looks wrong.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:19.300
Thousands of pages. Hundreds of authors.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.400
A picture with no description.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.400
A heading that is only bold text.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.400
Grey text on a white page.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.400
A table with no header row.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.600
The screen reader says “graphic.” Then moves on.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.400
No heading announced. No table headers.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.000
ADA Title II web rule: WCAG 2.1 AA.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.400
Due April 2027 or 2028, by population.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.400
Exceptions are narrow. Ask counsel about your wiki.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Fixed, with a dated record.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.200
Each page checked as it is written.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.800
Clarable. Check every page. Keep the record.

